-- title:
--   Errors of subtree evaluations with labelled leaves
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. An ordered tree has finite levels $0,1,2,\dots$ with a single root, and monotone surjective parent maps from level $k+1$ to level $k$; edge weights are positive and sum to $1$ over the children of each parent. Each node carries a nonexpansive selfmap of $K$, and the tree is evaluated bottom-up: a node's value is its map applied to the weighted average of its children's values. Fix a tree evaluation, an input $x$, and suppose every child average of the labels returns near $x$: $\|\sum_{\mathrm{par}(c)=p}w(c)f_{d+1,c}(x)-x\|\le\tau_d$ for all parents $p$ at level $d<N$.
--
--   1. **One collapse.** $\|\mathrm{collapse}(H)(p)-b\|\le\sum_cw(c)\|H(c)-b\|+\|f_p(b)-b\|$, and the analogous comparison with the label $f_p(x)$.
--   2. **Labelled subtree.** If the leaves at level $N$ below $v$ (level $k$) carry their labels $f_{N,s}(x)$, then
--   $$
--   \bigl\|\mathrm{sub}_{k,N}(H)(v)-f_{k,v}(x)\bigr\|\le\sum_{d=k}^{N-1}\tau_d .
--   $$
--   Only equality on the descendant leaves of $v$ is needed.
